-- Traction as a straight grip MULTIPLIER: 0.75 زلق · 1.00 عادي (= the car as its author built
-- it) · 1.80 خشن. CSP only gives us physics.setGripDecrease, documented as "0 for tyres to act
-- as usual, 1 for tyres to lose all grip" — a reduction. So decrease = 1 - grp: 0.75 -> 0.25 and
-- 1.00 -> 0 are exact, while 1.80 -> -0.8 leans on a negative value the docs never mention. If
-- CSP clamps it, خشن just feels like عادي — no harm, and the old code's alternative was worse:
-- it sold "عادي" at 0.75x, so every car on the server felt permanently broken.
local function applyGrip() pcall(function() physics.setGripDecrease(0, ac.Wheel.All, 1 - grp) end) end
